+# Governance & Runbook: Aegis operator guide (escalation, evidence, roles)
+
+Overview
+- This runbook documents operator responsibilities, escalation flow, evidence retention and reviewer interaction.
+
+Roles
+- Platform Owner: manages COSIGN_KMS_URI, REKOR_SERVER, MLflow, S3 evidence buckets.
+- Safety Officer: signs approvals for high-risk actions, reviews HIL/RT runs.
+- Controls Lead: responsible for controller code, HIL tests and formal specs.
+- Infra Operator: provisions/hardens self-hosted runners and deploys autoscaler/provisioners.
+
+Escalation flow
+1. Alert (Prometheus/Grafana) -> Platform Owner notified (PagerDuty)  
+2. If RT/HIL SLO breach -> Safety Officer + Controls Lead engaged; freeze promotions.  
+3. If supply-chain anomaly (unsigned image) -> Infra Operator blocks promotion and initiates recovery.
+
+Evidence retention
+- All auditor bundles (.tar.gz) and cosign signatures must be stored in S3 under s3://aegis-evidence/YYYY-MM-DD/<run-id>/ and retained per org policy (e.g., 365 days).
+- MLflow runs and evidence_sdk manifests must be backed up and accessible to certifiers.
+
+Approval policy
+- High-risk actuator commands require Safety Officer approval via approval service and produce cosign-signed approval artifacts.
+
+Checklist for auditor submission
+- RT SLO proof JSON, jitter samples, safe-stop traces  
+- HIL bundle (waveforms, contact injection traces) signed with cosign  
+- TLA+ specs + Apalache outputs (counterexample triage)  
+- NPU readiness reports and builder evidence (cosign + Rekor entries)  
+- CI promotion gate logs demonstrating supply-chain enforcement
+
